=== (ii) gauge-mode relations of the divergent parts ===
Let Phi_d solve Phi_d'' + 4 Phi_d'/eta = K_SPhi^(-n) = (K_Q^(-n))'/eta with Phi_d(0) = K_Phi2(0)^(-n) (regular, unique).
Then r := eta Phi_d' + 3 Phi_d - Q_d has r' = eta(Phi_d'' + 4Phi_d'/eta - Q_d'/eta) = 0 and r(0) = 3Phi_d(0) - Q_d(0) = 0 (checked above):
   => Q_d = eta Phi_d' + 3 Phi_d for all eta, i.e. with G := eta Phi_d:  Phi_d = G/eta, Psi_d = Phi_d - Q_d = -(G' + G/eta).
delta2 divergent part (S00 has no divergent part; -2 eta^2 k^2 Phi/3 is O(k^0)): 4*Phi_d(eta)  (= 4 Phi_d = -4 G/eta... time-reparametrisation value)
v2_z divergent part (S0z regular): I*eta*k*Phi_d(eta)   = i k (eta Phi_d)  => V_d = eta Phi_d = G
engine (gauge.py, eta_old = eta + F(eta) P(x), F = -G): Psi + (eta Phi)' + Phi = 0

